From 6525de4bf7661aad37966d71fe5e9504d98cb1d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SlippyGetBackHere <343265862+SlippyGetBackHere@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:51:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cpu: optional main-CPU clock scale (overclock)

Add g_snes_cpu_clock_q8 (256 = console speed) and SNES_CPU_CLOCKS(),
and route every 65816 master-clock charge through it: the interpreter's
per-opcode charge and every charge the emitter writes into compiled
blocks. The beam, APU, DMA and coprocessors keep real time, so a value
below 256 makes the CPU faster without changing the frame rate or the
music. At 256 the charge is unchanged and generated code behaves
byte-for-byte as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 recompiler/v2/codegen.py        |  2 +-
 recompiler/v2/emit_function.py  | 14 +++++++-------
 runner/src/cpu_state.c          |  2 ++
 runner/src/cpu_state.h          |  9 +++++++++
 runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

